        "proposal": {
          "explanation": "All eight candidates target the SPI clock divider load conditions in llsdspi (lines 142, 144, 170). The public trace shows o_sck toggling high at cycle 102 when expected is 0, then repeated mismatches through cycle 110. The root cause is premature loading of r_clk_counter with i_speed during startup or early byte_accepted, before the low-level SPI engine (r_idle, CS, bus grant) is ready to drive SCK. Each patch adds a qualifying guard (i_cs, i_bus_grant, r_idle, !i_cs) to the relevant if/else-if branch so the divider only arms when a transaction is genuinely selected and the engine is idle. Patches at line 142 guard the startup_hold counter decrement; patches at line 144 guard the (startup_hold || byte_accepted) load in the else-if chain; patches at line 170 guard the same load in the main always block. The ranking orders by proximity to the observed failure: line 170 is the active divider load during normal operation, line 144 is the else-if counterpart, and line 142 is the startup path. Within each line, guards that match the trace's inactive inputs (i_cs=0, i_bus_grant=0, r_idle=0) are ranked higher.",
