            {
              "failure_port": "o_sck",
              "id": "patch_475847e36fa1",
              "mechanism": "The original r_clk_counter load condition at line 170 unconditionally loads i_speed when (startup_hold || byte_accepted) is true. In the failing trace, byte_accepted becomes asserted at cycle 94 (via i_wb_stb with o_idle), causing r_clk_counter to be loaded immediately. However, the SPI clock (o_sck) should not begin toggling until the low-level state machine has sequenced past startup and is ready to drive SCK low/high. The patch adds && (!i_cs) to this gate so the divider only loads when chip-select is asserted, preventing premature counter loads and aligning o_sck with the expected idle-high behavior.",
              "source_line": 170
            },
            {
              "failure_port": "o_sck",
              "id": "patch_baa9767c5bfd",
              "mechanism": "At line 144, the counter load branch for (startup_hold || byte_accepted) lacks a chip-select guard. If byte_accepted fires while i_cs is de-asserted (idle bus), the divider loads i_speed and r_z_counter becomes active, which later qualifies SCK transitions. Adding && (!i_cs) ensures the divider only arms when a transaction is actually selected, matching the observed need for o_sck to stay low during early cycles.",
              "source_line": 144
